<!-- ── MAIN CONTENT ── -->
<div class="main-wrap" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">

  <main style="max-width: 760px;">

    <div class="article-content">
      <h2>Why HELOCEdge.com Exists</h2>
      <p>Home Equity Lines of Credit are one of the most commonly searched, and most commonly misunderstood, financial products available to American homeowners. Lenders advertise the appealing parts, draw-period flexibility, lower starting rates, but the fine print around variable rates, repayment-period payment jumps, and combined loan-to-value limits often gets glossed over.</p>
      <p>HELOCEdge.com was built to fix that. Every calculator on this site exists to answer one specific, practical question a homeowner might be asking themselves before they ever speak to a lender, in plain English, with no sales pitch attached.</p>

      <h2>Who's Behind This Site</h2>
      <p>HELOCEdge.com is an independent publication researched, written, and maintained by Mike Lucas. Mike is based in the UK and has spent years building informational, education-first websites covering personal finance topics for a US audience. He has no lending background and no financial industry affiliation; his focus is purely on researching publicly available information, government and industry data sources, and presenting it clearly.</p>
      <p>AI writing tools are used to help research and draft content more efficiently, with all output reviewed and edited before publishing. This disclosure is included on every page of the site in the interest of transparency.</p>

      <div class="callout callout-tip">
        <i class="ti ti-shield-check"></i>
        <div class="callout-content">
          <strong>No lender relationships</strong>
          <p>HELOCEdge.com does not partner with, receive commission from, or have any financial relationship with any lender, bank, or financial institution. The calculators and content here are not influenced by advertising or sponsorship from any financial company.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How the Calculators Work</h2>
      <p>Every calculator on this site uses standard, publicly documented financial formulas, the same amortization and loan-to-value calculations lenders themselves use internally. None of the figures produced are guarantees or offers of credit; they are estimates intended to help you understand your situation before discussing it with a licensed professional.</p>

      <h2>Our Approach to Accuracy</h2>
      <p>Where this site references current rates or market data, it links directly to primary sources, such as Freddie Mac's published mortgage rate data, rather than displaying static figures that quickly become outdated. Content is reviewed periodically to ensure it reflects current lending practices and terminology.</p>

      <h2>Questions or Feedback?</h2>
      <p>If you spot an error, have a suggestion for a new calculator, or just want to get in touch, visit the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> — Mike reads every message personally.</p>
    </div>

  </main>

</div>

